-f51c-45e9-8fd1-91b225480722"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"faca1da3a97e872d5fffc5fb261d1305af0d25369bbf9a0254dbe946441c591f","event_uuid":"09f183e5-b748-4949-a44f-76749b2c8427","position":{"commit_sha":"23f7253c664fff3d8952ddab86eddcc317abfd2b","position":"1786609832767365001-09f183e5-b748-4949-a44f-76749b2c8427"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause CONFIRMED on current main (worktree bluebottle2-gitretry, branched from origin/main).\n\nRead the retry family in src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:\n- run_git_write composes _with_index_lock_retry (OUTER, git lock signatures) around _with_transient_head_retry (INNER).\n- _with_transient_head_retry matches only _is_transient_head_error, whose marker sets are _TRANSIENT_HEAD_MARKERS = ('could not parse head',) and _TRANSIENT_OBJECT_MARKERS = ('bad object',). Both are READ-side signatures (HEAD parse, parse_object returning NULL).\n- Neither substring matches git's write-side loose-object temp-create fault ('unable to create temporary file' / 'failed to insert into database' / 'unable to index file'), so run_git_write returns that failure on its first attempt.\n\nConfirmed the asymmetric counterpart: src/rebar/_store/event_append.py defines _TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS with exactly those three write-side markers, wrapped by _with_transient_add_retry, and composes it ONLY into event_append's own _git_add / _git_commit / _git_commit_paths and the two recovery commits. Grep over src confirms no other module references that family, so every non-event_append caller of the shared seam (s3_doctor, which imports run_git_write and is_transient_object_read_error; compaction; the claim/transition writers) is unprotected against the write-side fault class.\n\nSo the asymmetry the bug describes is real and present: the identical runner-FS fault self-heals on the git add path and hard-fails on the shared write seam. Proceeding to fix by moving the write-side marker family into gitutil so there is ONE definition and every run_git_write caller inherits the bounded retry.","timestamp":1786603763718337001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree bluebottle2-gitretry.\n\ngitutil: added _TRANSIENT_WRITE_MARKERS (the three write-side markers, moved verbatim from event_append) plus the module-private _is_transient_object_write_error predicate; folded it into the transient classifier, which is renamed _is_transient_head_error -> _is_transient_git_fault and _with_transient_head_retry -> _with_transient_fault_retry (constants renamed to _TRANSIENT_FAULT_ATTEMPTS / _TRANSIENT_FAULT_BACKOFF_S) since the loop is no longer HEAD-specific. The retry gained the attempts keyword event_append's private loop had. Budget, backoff and return-immediately-on-anything-else behaviour are unchanged; corrupt-object signatures still excluded.\n\nevent_append: deleted _TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS, the private predicate body and _with_transient_add_retry; _is_transient_add_error is now a re-export of the shared predicate (one definition), and all five composition sites plus _git_add route through _with_transient_fault_retry. This also collapses the accidental 3x3 nested budget on the commit paths to the intended bounded 3.\n\nTests: new tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py covers the ENOENT retry through run_git_write, the macOS EINVAL spelling, each sibling marker, the corrupt-object/index.lock exclusions, budget exhaustion returning the failing result, s3_doctor._git inheriting the retry, and the single-definition identity. tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py repointed at the renamed predicate. No timing assertions; backoff stubbed.\n\nGates green locally: all check_* gates, complexity baseline, generators no-diff, make lint, make typecheck. Full CI pytest tier running.","timestamp":1786605386170159001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Rebased onto origin/main (5f4a5c1d40, 'Split fsck by concern into scan and health'). No conflicting gitutil changes from the in-flight clone-compactor story had landed, so the rebase was clean. Commit dd74672bf8 (pre-push). Re-running the CI pytest tier on the rebased tree before pushing to Gerrit.","timestamp":1786605479992373001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit as change 1713 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1713), commit dd74672bf8 on top of origin/main 5f4a5c1d40.\n\nLocal CI pytest tier on the rebased tree: 12668 passed, 52 skipped, 1 failed — tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count, a log-capture assertion in a file this change does not touch (it belongs to the just-landed inbound-removal-confirmation work). It passes in isolation (10/10), so it is a parallel-run flake, not a regression from this change. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1786607323284949001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: change 1713 merged as c8a380e24ccb0eac634a9dcf5f13f4badf44bdd7 (Gerrit rebased it server-side onto b4b8519c66 and submitted). LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) and Verified +1 (rebar CI bot) before submit.\n\nWorktree realigned to the merged tip; the three affected test files (43 tests) pass on the merged tree. All acceptance criteria ticked.","timestamp":1786609412031290001}],"created_at":1786601411942075001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"856b44c7-564d-4038-a25a-756f1b662554","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"cfcb-a023-09a0-42ad"},{"link_uuid":"b1591dbd-05f3-46df-a563-43422e46c4b2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a539-e0d6-d542-4b55"}],"description":"## Problem\nA write-side transient runner-FS fault aborts store git operations routed through\n`gitutil.run_git_write`, because that seam's transient-retry family covers only READ-side\nsignatures. The identical fault is already recognised and retried on `event_append`'s\n`git add` path, so the store self-heals in one place and red-lights CI in another.\n\nSymptom (bug `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle`): the s3 doctor's `git commit-tree` failed with\n`error: unable to create temporary file: No such file or directory`, aborting\n`tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py::test_heal_folds_into_the_ref_from_a_detached_head_tracker`\nwith `S3DoctorConflict`. One CI shard only; the same code passed on every other shard and\nlocally — the fingerprint of a runner-FS blip, not a data fault.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed on current main)\n- `gitutil.run_git_write` composes `_with_index_lock_retry` (OUTER, git lock signatures)\n  around `_with_transient_head_retry` (INNER).\n- `_with_transient_head_retry` retries only what `_is_transient_head_error` matches:\n  `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_MARKERS` (`could not parse head`) and `_TRANSIENT_OBJECT_MARKERS`\n  (`bad object`). Both are READ-side faults.\n- The write-side loose-object temp-create signature matches neither, so `run_git_write`\n  returns it on the first attempt.\n- `event_append._TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS` + `_with_transient_add_retry` DO match it, but are\n  composed only into `event_append`'s `_git_add`, `_git_commit`, `_git_commit_paths` and its\n  two recovery commits. Every other `run_git_write` caller — `s3_doctor`, compaction, the\n  claim/transition writers — is unprotected.\n\n## Approach\nMove the write-side marker family into the shared seam and delete the private copy, so there\nis exactly ONE definition and every store git caller inherits the same bounded retry. No new\nheuristic dialect: the marker strings are carried over verbatim from `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS`\nand the attempt/backoff shape stays the existing bounded 3-attempt, linear-backoff loop.\n\nIn `gitutil`:\n- Add `_TRANSIENT_WRITE_MARKERS` (the three verbatim write-side markers) and a\n  module-private `_is_transient_object_write_error` predicate over them. Kept private, not\n  public like `is_transient_object_read_error`: that one is public because `s3_doctor` folds\n  a hint from it in production, and the write-side predicate has no such production caller —\n  only the retry loop and `event_append`'s re-export. It can be promoted if one appears.\n- Fold it into the transient predicate, renaming `_is_transient_head_error` ->\n  `_is_transient_git_fault` and `_with_transient_head_retry` -> `_with_transient_fault_retry`\n  (with `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_ATTEMPTS`/`_TRANSIENT_HEAD_BACKOFF_S` renamed to match), because the\n  loop is no longer HEAD-specific. Mechanical rename; the loop body, budget and\n  return-immediately-on-anything-else behaviour are unchanged.\n- Give `_with_transient_fault_retry` the `attempts` keyword `_with_transient_add_retry`\n  already had, so `_git_add`'s pass-through survives the merge.\n\nIn `event_append`:\n- Delete `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS`, `_is_transient_add_error` and `_with_transient_add_retry`;\n  re-export the shared `_is_transient_object_write_error` under the existing\n  `_is_transient_add_error` name so the current classification test keeps a symbol to assert\n  on.\n- Replace each nested `_with_transient_head_retry(lambda: _with_transient_add_retry(f))`\n  composition with a single `_with_transient_fault_retry(f)`, and route `_git_add` through it\n  too. This is a deliberate narrowing of an accidental budget: the nested pair currently gives\n  the commit paths up to 3x3 attempts on a write fault; one loop restores the intended bounded\n  3, the same budget the read-side faults get.\n\nIdempotence precondition is already satisfied and documented: `run_git_write`'s docstring\nrequires it, and `add`/`commit`/`commit-tree` are content-addressed re-writes of the same\nobjects on the same state.\n\nExclusions preserved: the corrupt-object signatures the existing comments call out\n(`loose object ... is corrupt`, `inflate: data stream error`) are still not matched, and a\nwrite fault that survives the whole budget still returns its failing result, so a genuinely\npersistent fault fails loudly.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — shared write-side marker family + predicate; rename the\n  now-general transient retry.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — delete the private copy; adopt the shared retry at its\n  five composition sites and in `_git_add`.\n- `tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py` — new regression tests.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py` — repoint the two\n  classification assertions at the surviving symbol (behaviour assertions untouched).\n- `tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py` — MUST be edited by the rename: it imports\n  `_is_transient_head_error` from `gitutil` and asserts on it, so it is repointed at\n  `_is_transient_git_fault`. Without this edit the rename breaks the module's import and\n  fails collection of every test it holds.\n\nOut of scope, not touched: `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`.\n\n## Testing\nNew unit tests drive `run_git_write` with a fake `run_git` seam that returns a scripted\nsequence of `CompletedProcess` results, counting attempts (no sleeps asserted, no timing\nbudgets):\n- Linux ENOENT write-side stderr on attempt 1, success on attempt 2 -> `run_git_write` returns\n  the success and made exactly 2 attempts.\n- macOS EINVAL spelling and each sibling marker (`failed to insert into database`,\n  `unable to index file`) are classified transient by `is_transient_object_write_error`.\n- A corrupt-object stderr (`loose object ... is corrupt`) is NOT retried: exactly 1 attempt,\n  failing result returned.\n- A write-side fault on EVERY attempt returns the failing result after the bounded budget and\n  does not loop forever.\n- The s3 doctor inherits it: its git op driven through the seam with the fault injected once\n  completes instead of raising.\n`test_event_append_transient_retry.py` and `test_run_git_wrapper.py` must still pass after\ntheir symbol references are repointed (see Scope), proving the `git add` and read-side\nbehaviours are unchanged after de-duplication.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `run_git_write` retries a write-side temp-file ENOENT/EINVAL failure — a test injects the\n      failure on the first attempt and asserts the call succeeds on retry.\n- [x] The s3 doctor inherits it — a test drives a doctor git op through the seam with the fault\n      injected once and asserts it completes instead of raising.\n- [x] Corrupt-object signatures are still NOT retried — a test asserts immediate surfacing.\n- [x] A write-side fault that survives the bounded budget still returns its failing result.\n- [x] The renamed symbols have no stale references — `tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py` is\n      repointed and the full unit suite collects and passes.\n- [x] The write-side marker family has exactly one definition — a grep finds no second copy,\n      and `event_append`'s `git add` retry still passes its existing tests.\n- [x] The full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"recognise write-side temp-file transient signatures in the shared retry so every store git caller inherits them"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"reuse the shared marker family in _git_add instead of a private copy"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py","reason":"tests for the retried write-side fault, the corrupt-object exclusion, and the budget"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","a539-e0d6-d542-4b55"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8679ea5e-f51c-45e9-8fd1-91b225480722","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f7da-baae-3c93-47e2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Shared git seam does not retry write-side temp-file faults","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5cb7204c-3640-4637-bb7d-dc90f051c591","db15ec1c-ee2b-4c61-a9a9-ec3304adca75","856b44c7-564d-4038-a25a-756f1b662554","3323a761-045e-4171-8c2a-29c400eb7e8f","3b7c4260-aec8-4fc5-8025-86325c2ba9e2","d7e68f03-6932-46d2-9f50-c24801dd4384","2aa26a0c-a222-4176-b4e8-40eadd152644","dcab5dab-4b6d-438e-a3f2-aed2614c80fc","883b216e-2453-4100-8424-c93310dcbf65","16a1584a-fea4-4b58-9760-a61bfb2be063","dec90b1f-67f4-485d-a992-6d6c2ac72fce","945731a8-691d-46df-8ea1-8d80b9bfee7d","b1591dbd-05f3-46df-a563-43422e46c4b2","4d08da74-de83-4b44-85b3-b57b3780f6b1","4c28d1f9-bf27-4dba-9def-c43b8be04f5e","8679ea5e-f51c-45e9-8fd1-91b225480722","09f183e5-b748-4949-a44f-76749b2c8427"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659695981573001,"uuid":"ec90920c-5b14-41bb-bcf5-092190932acf"}